{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"/*\\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\\n\\n    The stencil calculation stops when  ( err >= CONV_THRESHOLD OR  iter > ITER_MAX )\\n*/\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <time.h>\\n#include <sys/time.h>\\n\\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f // threshold of convergence\\n\\n// matrix to be solved\\ndouble **grid;\\n\\n// auxiliary matrix\\ndouble **new_grid;\\n\\n// size of each side of the grid\\nint size;\\nint iter_max_num;\\n\\n// return the absolute value of a number\\ndouble absolute(double num){\\n    if(num < 0)\\n        return -1.0 * num;\\n    return num;\\n}\\n\\n\\n// allocate memory for the grid\\nvoid allocate_memory(){\\n    grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\\n    new_grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\\n\\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\\n        new_grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// initialize the grid\\nvoid initialize_grid(){\\n    int center = size / 2;\\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++){\\n            // inicializa região de calor no centro do grid\\n            if ( i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup)\\n                grid[i][j] = 100;\\n            else\\n                grid[i][j] = 0;\\n            new_grid[i][j] = 0.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// save the grid in a file\\nvoid save_grid(){\\n\\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\\n            fprintf(stdout, \\\"%lf \\\", grid[i][j]);\\n        }\\n        fprintf(stdout, \\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]){\\n\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &size);\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &iter_max_num);\\n    \\n    int hasError = 1;\\n    int iter = 0;\\n\\n    struct timeval time_start;\\n    struct timeval time_end;\\n\\n    // allocate memory to the grid (matrix)\\n    allocate_memory();\\n\\n    // set grid initial conditions\\n    initialize_grid();\\n\\n    //printf(\\\"Jacobi relaxation calculation: %d x %d grid\\\\n\\\", size, size);\\n\\n    // get the start time\\n    //gettimeofday(&time_start, NULL);\\n\\n    // Keep one team across timesteps. Each timestep completes the stencil,\\n    // convergence reduction, and copy before any thread begins the next one.\\n    #pragma omp parallel\\n    {\\n        // Jacobi iteration\\n        // This loop will end if either the maximum change reaches below a set threshold (convergence)\\n        // or a fixed number of maximum iterations have completed\\n        while ( hasError && iter < iter_max_num ) {\\n\\n            #pragma omp single\\n            hasError = 0;\\n\\n            // Each row is independent while reading grid; SIMD lanes update\\n            // distinct new_grid cells. The integer OR reductions combine only\\n            // whether any cell exceeded the convergence threshold.\\n            #pragma omp for schedule(static) reduction(|:hasError)\\n            for( int i = 1; i < size-1; i++) {\\n                int row_has_error = 0;\\n                #pragma omp simd reduction(|:row_has_error)\\n                for(int j = 1; j < size-1; j++) {\\n\\n                    new_grid[i][j] = 0.25 * (grid[i][j+1] + grid[i][j-1] +\\n                                             grid[i-1][j] + grid[i+1][j]);\\n\\n                    double errorCurrent = absolute(new_grid[i][j] - grid[i][j]);\\n                    if(errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD ){\\n                        row_has_error |= 1;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                hasError |= row_has_error;\\n            }\\n\\n            // The preceding worksharing loop's barrier ensures all new values\\n            // are ready before any thread copies them into the working grid.\\n            #pragma omp for simd collapse(2) schedule(static)\\n            for( int i = 1; i < size-1; i++) {\\n                for( int j = 1; j < size-1; j++) {\\n                    grid[i][j] = new_grid[i][j];\\n                }\\n            }\\n\\n            #pragma omp single\\n            iter++;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    // get the end time\\n    //gettimeofday(&time_end, NULL);\\n\\n    //double exec_time = (double) (time_end.tv_sec - time_start.tv_sec) +\\n    //                   (double) (time_end.tv_usec - time_start.tv_usec) / 1000000.0;\\n\\n    //save the final grid in file\\n    save_grid();\\n\\n    //printf(\\\"\\\\nKernel executed in %lf seconds with %d iterations.\\\\n\\\", exec_time, iter);\\n\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/laplace_seq.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"A persistent OpenMP team with static row scheduling and legal SIMD across the independent contiguous column updates may improve stencil throughput on the four-core ARM64 target while preserving the Jacobi iteration and convergence semantics.\",\"notes\":\"This is an unmeasured hypothesis. The controller should verify that OpenMP is enabled in the build and evaluate correctness and speed across valid inputs.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Keep a single OpenMP parallel region across iterations; distribute independent stencil rows with static scheduling and combine convergence flags using integer OR reductions.\",\"Apply SIMD to the independent inner-column stencil loop and the independent collapsed copy loop, retaining barriers between stencil computation, convergence decision, copying, and the next iteration.\"]}"}}
